      "20.2 Events of default. Each of the following constitutes an event of default by the Party concerned: (a) failure to pay any amount due for two (2) consecutive Settlement Periods, or any amount overdue by more than sixty (60) days; (b) material breach of any obligation under this Agreement not remedied within the applicable cure period; (c) persistent failure to maintain the service levels in Clause 14 continuing for thirty (30) days after written notice; (d) the commencement of any insolvency, winding-up, bankruptcy or corporate insolvency resolution proceeding which is not dismissed within sixty (60) days; (e) any representation under Clause 18 proving to have been materially untrue when made; or (f) conviction of the Party or its proprietor, partner, director or principal officer for any offence involving moral turpitude or fraud.",
